# Machine-readable evidence and readable complete operation index.
with (out/'CREDENTIAL-WRITE-INVENTORY.json').open('x') as f:json.dump(rows,f,indent=2)
intro='''# Credential and account-authority write inventory

Source review of all three development projects. Paths are relative to the existing /<API_ROUTES> mount; no production prefix or reachability is assumed. Database connections were not opened. JSON companion records exact routes, complete middleware argument lists, controller anchors, queries, independent proof, classifications and authentication matrix.

C means source-confirmed unauthorized credential mutation/issuance/deletion at the application boundary, including explicit provider secrets. E means source-confirmed unprotected authority grant. Neither label claims a live exploit. P marks missing proof, indirect effects or uncertainty; it does not erase a source-confirmed non-credential integrity issue. A is scoped to the existing terminal recovery denial, not global security. U (unresolved trusted data) applies to reopening privileged writes generally: existing mutable roles/membership/status are not an independently trusted grant source. These labels are not mutually exclusive.

Every legacy authCheck below uses decode only (no signature or expiration verification). adminGratisCheck adds a current row lookup by unverified email + caller-selected primary store and admits cashier/moderator/admin. No such route therefore has a verified actor just because it has two middleware names. Explicit target predicates and independent old-password/code predicates are retained in the evidence rather than treated as nonexistent.

'''
parts=[intro]
for r in rows:
 parts += [f"## {r['id']} — {r['function']} ({r['priority']})\n\n",'Routes: '+ '; '.join(f"`{b['method']} {b['path']}`" for b in r['routes'])+'.\n\n',f"Source: `{r['project']}/{r['route_file']}`; `{r['controller']}:{r['controller_line']}`.\n\n",f"- Bound chain: {r['routes']}.\n- Database/issuance: {r['write']}.\n- Scope: {r['query_scope']}.\n- Independent permission/proof: {r['independent_proof_or_permission']}.\n- Classification: {'; '.join(r['classification'])}.\n- Impact/limit: {r['impact']}\n\n"]
parts.append('''## Other inspected surfaces and exclusions

Main controllers/user.js sendEmail and handleWorkflow1 relay outbound mail/subscriber requests; no local credential write. Neither is a trusted recovery issuer. Main customerRoutes.js returns mock customer/license/access objects: database operations are commented out, license keys are generated/returned but no authoritative verifier/storage is implemented; authentication/entitlement use is unresolved, not a confirmed User password writer. AI migrate.js imports User but its User operations are commented read-only image migration, not credential mutation; migration endpoints are not run. Main models/app/user.js is a shadow schema with the same GratisUser model name; active app controller imports ../.. /models/user (without the space), not this shadow model. AI user model/guard similarly does not imply a credential write in image handlers.

Store counter writes in main app/order.js and joborder.js are explicit cart/order/jobs marker updates; they do not directly change store identity, reseller ownership, role or password. Other controller models (products, orders, addresses, points, cashflow, jobs, categories, brands, events, payments) were searched for User aliases, raw collection writes, password assignments and authority updates. Payment credentials and billing metadata are included above. No other active User mutation was found in application source. Generated/runtime/test/doc/vendor files are not application endpoints; full integrity manifests cover their unchanged bytes. MUTATION-SCAN.json is the discovery/evidence cross-check, not an AST proof of every possible dynamic dataflow.

Frontend has no authoritative database credential writer: functions/user.js and auth.js submit requests and persist returned tokens/user data in browser state/storage. Their callers matter for migration and are in COMPATIBILITY.md. No client guard is counted as server authorization. Scanner session endpoint uses cryptographic checks and fresh proof in its isolated design, but is disabled and is not a credential-change endpoint; current authority data remains vulnerable to the other writers. Its local checks do not make mutable legacy roles trustworthy.
''')
with (out/'CREDENTIAL-WRITE-INVENTORY.md').open('x') as f:f.write(''.join(parts))
# Pins for every inspected application JS file (excluding generated image payload directories).
pins=[];mutations=[]
for project,root in [('main',main),('ai',ai)]:
 for folder in ['routes','controllers','middlewares','models','services','dbconnect','config']:
  for p in sorted((root/folder).rglob('*.js')):
   if 'product-images' in p.parts:continue
   b=p.read_bytes();s=b.decode(errors='replace');rel=str(p.relative_to(root));pins.append({'project':project,'path':rel,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()})
   for m in re.finditer(r'\b(?:User|GratisUser|Estore|Payment|Billing)\.(?:findOneAndUpdate|findByIdAndUpdate|updateOne|updateMany|findOneAndDelete|deleteMany|bulkWrite|insertMany|create)\s*\(|new (?:User|Estore|Payment|Billing)\s*\(|jwt\.sign\s*\(',s):
    prev=list(re.finditer(r'exports\.(\w+)\s*=',s[:m.start()]));fn=prev[-1][1] if prev else '(helper/module)'
    mutations.append({'project':project,'file':rel,'line':s[:m.start()].count('\n')+1,'function':fn,'expression':m[0],'inventory_ids':[r['id'] for r in rows if r['project']==project and r['controller']==rel and r['function']==fn]})
 for rel in ['server.js','package.json','package-lock.json']:
  p=root/rel
  if p.exists():pins.append({'project':project,'path':rel,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()})
for p in sorted((front/'src').rglob('*')):
 if p.is_file() and p.suffix in ['.js','.jsx','.ts','.tsx']:pins.append({'project':'frontend','path':str(p.relative_to(front)),'sha256':hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()})
with (out/'SOURCE-EVIDENCE.json').open('x') as f:json.dump(pins,f,indent=2)
with (out/'MUTATION-SCAN.json').open('x') as f:json.dump(mutations,f,indent=2)
print('Inventoried',len(rows),'operations;',len(pins),'source hashes;',len(mutations),'mutation/issuance anchors')
print('Unmapped anchors:',json.dumps([r for r in mutations if not r['inventory_ids']],indent=2))
